1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,760
 Et, please, we welcome your questions tonight.

2
00:00:02,880 --> 00:00:03,160
 Thank you.

3
00:00:04,220 --> 00:00:05,520
 Merci beaucoup, Monsieur McQueen.

4
00:00:05,640 --> 00:00:06,540
 Monsieur Théodore Rescot.

5
00:00:06,960 --> 00:00:07,880
 Merci, Madame la Mairese.

6
00:00:08,020 --> 00:00:08,520
 Hi, everybody.

7
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:10,440
 Good to be back after the summer break.

8
00:00:10,620 --> 00:00:13,800
 Happy to see our colleague, Peter McQueen, back on stage with us.

9
00:00:14,140 --> 00:00:16,140
 Prond rétablissement, mon cher collègue.

10
00:00:16,280 --> 00:00:17,720
 Je souhaite que tu t'en remettes très vite.

11
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:21,440
 So, a few files that I'd like to follow up on,

12
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:25,080
 on the stuff that we did at the borough level in the past few months.

13
00:00:25,520 --> 00:00:28,340
 One, and I'm particularly proud to say that we're moving ahead.

14
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:33,220
 After 30 years of inaction from past administration is the Empress Project.

15
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:36,980
 As you know, there has been a public consultation.

16
00:00:37,080 --> 00:00:37,840
 It's still going on.

17
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:40,900
 And we're going to talk about democracy later in the motion.

18
00:00:41,300 --> 00:00:43,880
 And this is just one example of all the different ways

19
00:00:43,880 --> 00:00:46,240
 that we can actually consult with the population.

20
00:00:46,980 --> 00:00:49,600
 And one that is going on now until the 20th of September

21
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:53,560
 is the online survey that you can access through the website.

22
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:58,320
 And also, we've been with our population on the streets

23
00:00:58,320 --> 00:01:03,340
 at Imagine Monkland to collect more than about 100 responses

24
00:01:03,340 --> 00:01:07,080
 of what should happen there during the transition phase.

25
00:01:08,120 --> 00:01:11,140
 Don't forget, there's a big consultation evening

26
00:01:11,140 --> 00:01:13,660
 happening at the Parc du Chalet, Le Rendez-vous,

27
00:01:14,120 --> 00:01:16,660
 in Parc NDG, in front of the Empress,

28
00:01:17,040 --> 00:01:20,380
 on the 14th of September at 7 p.m.

29
00:01:20,720 --> 00:01:23,100
 So show up early and in numbers.

30
00:01:24,780 --> 00:01:28,180
 Just to let you know, we're still talking about the transition phase of this project.

31
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:30,500
 This is by no mean the final destination,

32
00:01:30,720 --> 00:01:33,040
 but this will be a way that we can move ahead.

33
00:01:33,340 --> 00:01:34,040
 Like we said,

34
00:01:34,220 --> 00:01:36,400
 manger à l'elephant une bouchée à la fois.

35
00:01:36,900 --> 00:01:37,940
 Can we say that in English?

36
00:01:38,240 --> 00:01:39,060
 Eat the elephant one?

37
00:01:39,180 --> 00:01:39,380
 Okay.

38
00:01:40,320 --> 00:01:42,800
 And so I'm very proud to say that we're moving ahead.

39
00:01:44,460 --> 00:01:48,020
 The second major project that we've polarized,

40
00:01:48,340 --> 00:01:50,340
 mobilized, and really occupied our minds

41
00:01:50,340 --> 00:01:51,680
 since we got into office

42
00:01:51,680 --> 00:01:52,700
 is in particular,

43
00:01:52,840 --> 00:01:53,920
 la piste cyclable Terrebonne.

44
00:01:53,920 --> 00:01:57,160
 and I know there are people are laughing,

45
00:01:57,320 --> 00:01:58,120
 people are angry.

46
00:01:58,540 --> 00:01:59,620
 It left no one,

47
00:01:59,720 --> 00:02:00,560
 especially in Loyola,

48
00:02:01,080 --> 00:02:03,240
 indifferent on the topic, right?

49
00:02:03,580 --> 00:02:06,020
 So I don't think there's one topic

50
00:02:06,020 --> 00:02:08,060
 that has been more present on the agenda

51
00:02:08,060 --> 00:02:09,980
 every week,

52
00:02:10,160 --> 00:02:11,680
 at every statutory meeting

53
00:02:11,680 --> 00:02:12,820
 that we have with the services.

54
00:02:13,560 --> 00:02:15,020
 It's really impressive,

55
00:02:15,160 --> 00:02:17,160
 the amount of energy that we spend on this,

56
00:02:17,220 --> 00:02:18,160
 because we know it's important.

57
00:02:18,300 --> 00:02:20,240
 It's something that we heard loud and clear

58
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:21,960
 when we were doing the campaign.

59
00:02:22,080 --> 00:02:24,600
 It's something that we took very seriously from day one.

60
00:02:25,120 --> 00:02:26,080
 Since day one,

61
00:02:26,260 --> 00:02:29,580
 we've looked at a dozen or more of scenarios.

62
00:02:30,360 --> 00:02:32,860
 Some of you maybe have seen me even recently,

63
00:02:33,740 --> 00:02:35,960
 like a weirdo with my tape,

64
00:02:36,160 --> 00:02:37,880
 measuring tape on different parts

65
00:02:37,880 --> 00:02:41,200
 of the biking path in our borough

66
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:43,700
 and across the city, actually,

67
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:45,640
 to see precedents and comparables.

68
00:02:45,940 --> 00:02:46,700
 You see me, right?

69
00:02:46,880 --> 00:02:47,400
 You saw me?

70
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:48,120
 Yeah, okay.

71
00:02:48,620 --> 00:02:49,240
 It's always me.

72
00:02:50,140 --> 00:02:52,140
 Just to give us the range

73
00:02:52,140 --> 00:02:53,800
 of possibilities and options,

74
00:02:54,140 --> 00:02:55,480
 and again, the objective here,

75
00:02:55,900 --> 00:02:58,540
 there is a path that is clear in front of me

76
00:02:58,540 --> 00:02:59,920
 that we need to find a way

77
00:02:59,920 --> 00:03:04,020
 to basically find a meeting ground

78
00:03:04,020 --> 00:03:06,200
 for people who need more access

79
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:07,080
 with their cars,

80
00:03:07,160 --> 00:03:07,720
 for their parking,

81
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:08,480
 for their needs,

82
00:03:08,860 --> 00:03:09,780
 accessibility needs,

83
00:03:09,820 --> 00:03:12,440
 and also preserve safety capacity

84
00:03:12,440 --> 00:03:14,280
 for active mobility

85
00:03:14,280 --> 00:03:15,700
 for our families especially.

86
00:03:16,380 --> 00:03:18,240
 So in the next couple of days,

87
00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:19,440
 we will have an update

88
00:03:19,440 --> 00:03:21,960
 because it's now at the final stage

89
00:03:21,960 --> 00:03:24,520
 of the study that we submitted recently

90
00:03:24,520 --> 00:03:25,240
 with the services,

91
00:03:25,340 --> 00:03:26,600
 and the services have promised us

92
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:29,020
 a final answer in the next few days.

93
00:03:29,540 --> 00:03:31,200
 So before the end of fall,

94
00:03:31,640 --> 00:03:34,020
 you will have our own orientation

95
00:03:34,020 --> 00:03:35,800
 on what's going to happen this winter

96
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:37,140
 with the Terrebonne bike path.

97
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:38,320
 So it's coming.

98
00:03:41,540 --> 00:03:42,820
 Another major project

99
00:03:42,820 --> 00:03:43,820
 that I'm very proud of

100
00:03:43,820 --> 00:03:45,200
 is in terms of housing,

101
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:47,940
 especially vulnerable populations, right?

102
00:03:48,160 --> 00:03:50,280
 And we all have to do our part,

103
00:03:50,420 --> 00:03:51,220
 and I'm very happy

104
00:03:51,220 --> 00:03:52,100
 that we've been included

105
00:03:52,100 --> 00:03:53,620
 in the pilot project

106
00:03:53,620 --> 00:03:56,940
 of 54 transitory units

107
00:03:56,940 --> 00:03:57,860
 for women,

108
00:03:58,260 --> 00:03:59,260
 des femmes vulnérables,

109
00:03:59,300 --> 00:03:59,960
 and it's going to happen

110
00:03:59,960 --> 00:04:01,540
 in my district of Loyola

111
00:04:01,540 --> 00:04:03,560
 in the West Haven community.

112
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:04,620
 And this was done,

113
00:04:04,720 --> 00:04:05,900
 I'm very proud of this project

114
00:04:05,900 --> 00:04:07,700
 because the speed and the cost

115
00:04:07,700 --> 00:04:10,240
 which are key to really solve,

116
00:04:10,380 --> 00:04:11,160
 trying to put a dent

117
00:04:11,160 --> 00:04:13,480
 in this massive housing shortage

118
00:04:13,480 --> 00:04:14,980
 and affordability crisis

119
00:04:14,980 --> 00:04:15,640
 that we have,

120
00:04:16,140 --> 00:04:17,340
 this is one way

121
00:04:17,340 --> 00:04:18,840
 of trying to tackle the issue.

122
00:04:19,320 --> 00:04:21,500
 And so 54 units are coming up

123
00:04:21,500 --> 00:04:22,900
 in the next few months

124
00:04:22,900 --> 00:04:24,060
 in this community,

125
00:04:24,480 --> 00:04:26,140
 and I think we can all be

126
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:26,900
 very, very proud

127
00:04:26,900 --> 00:04:27,820
 of that achievement.

128
00:04:27,980 --> 00:04:28,520
 So again,

129
00:04:28,520 --> 00:04:29,560
 something to follow up

130
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:30,420
 on very, very soon.

131
00:04:32,820 --> 00:04:34,040
 Just in terms of

132
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:35,960
 multitude of points,

133
00:04:36,160 --> 00:04:37,160
 I've had a privilege,

134
00:04:37,540 --> 00:04:38,440
 j'ai le privilège franchement

135
00:04:38,440 --> 00:04:39,640
 d'assister à des événements

136
00:04:39,640 --> 00:04:40,880
 fantastiques de la communauté

137
00:04:40,880 --> 00:04:41,420
 pendant l'été,

138
00:04:41,480 --> 00:04:42,020
 on peut le faire.

139
00:04:42,480 --> 00:04:43,960
 J'ai assisté au festival

140
00:04:43,960 --> 00:04:45,140
 interculturel de NDG.

141
00:04:45,600 --> 00:04:47,520
 Merci à votre équipe fantastique,

142
00:04:47,580 --> 00:04:47,760
 Hala,

143
00:04:48,160 --> 00:04:49,060
 pour l'organisation.

144
00:04:49,240 --> 00:04:50,100
 C'était fantastique

145
00:04:50,100 --> 00:04:50,660
 de voir toutes

146
00:04:50,660 --> 00:04:51,700
 ces différentes communautés,

147
00:04:51,760 --> 00:04:52,700
 puis c'est vraiment la richesse,

148
00:04:53,140 --> 00:04:53,680
 une des richesses

149
00:04:53,680 --> 00:04:54,260
 de notre communauté

150
00:04:54,260 --> 00:04:55,040
 à Codenage NDG.

151
00:04:55,140 --> 00:04:55,320
 On le dit,

152
00:04:55,320 --> 00:04:55,840
 on est très fiers

153
00:04:55,840 --> 00:04:56,660
 de notre diversité.

154
00:04:57,140 --> 00:04:58,500
 Strength is in our diversity,

155
00:04:58,520 --> 00:04:59,820
 et vraiment,

156
00:04:59,900 --> 00:05:00,400
 j'ai eu un moment

157
00:05:00,400 --> 00:05:01,260
 un peu émotionnel,

158
00:05:01,320 --> 00:05:02,040
 parce que quand je voyais

159
00:05:02,040 --> 00:05:02,480
 tous ces gens

160
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:03,180
 qui viennent de partout

161
00:05:03,180 --> 00:05:03,760
 dans le monde,

162
00:05:04,220 --> 00:05:05,180
 alors que quand on regarde

163
00:05:05,180 --> 00:05:06,060
 les médias sociaux,

164
00:05:06,160 --> 00:05:06,500
 quand on regarde

165
00:05:06,500 --> 00:05:07,300
 les médias de partout,

166
00:05:07,860 --> 00:05:09,240
 on a tendance à…

167
00:05:09,240 --> 00:05:10,240
 les gens veulent nous mettre

168
00:05:10,240 --> 00:05:11,300
 les uns contre les autres.

169
00:05:11,680 --> 00:05:11,840
 Et là,

170
00:05:11,840 --> 00:05:12,720
 j'ai trouvé un moment

171
00:05:12,720 --> 00:05:13,560
 de bonheur

172
00:05:13,560 --> 00:05:14,420
 où tout le monde,

173
00:05:14,660 --> 00:05:15,940
 les moins âgés,

174
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:16,620
 les plus âgés,

175
00:05:16,980 --> 00:05:17,960
 et de tous les horizons,

176
00:05:18,360 --> 00:05:19,220
 de toutes les couleurs,

177
00:05:19,340 --> 00:05:19,940
 étaient ensemble

178
00:05:19,940 --> 00:05:20,660
 pour célébrer

179
00:05:20,660 --> 00:05:21,960
 la force de notre communauté.

180
00:05:22,080 --> 00:05:22,920
 J'en étais très fier.

181
00:05:23,480 --> 00:05:24,700
 Et ça s'est reproduit aussi

182
00:05:24,700 --> 00:05:25,940
 durant Imagine Monkland,

183
00:05:26,320 --> 00:05:27,160
 durant Patrimoine,

184
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:27,500
 en fait,

185
00:05:27,560 --> 00:05:28,300
 où on a mis de l'avant

186
00:05:28,300 --> 00:05:29,880
 le 150e anniversaire

187
00:05:29,880 --> 00:05:30,520
 de NDG.

188
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:31,600
 J'en étais très fier aussi.

189
00:05:32,700 --> 00:05:33,360
 Et voilà.

190
00:05:33,920 --> 00:05:34,740
 Je vais finir là-dessus,

191
00:05:34,900 --> 00:05:36,180
 mais jeunesse Loyola,

192
00:05:36,820 --> 00:05:37,300
 s'il vous plaît,

193
00:05:37,860 --> 00:05:38,540
 je suis allé les voir.

194
00:05:38,800 --> 00:05:39,760
 Ils ont besoin de notre aide.

195
00:05:39,980 --> 00:05:40,300
 C'est le moment

196
00:05:40,300 --> 00:05:40,840
 de nous montrer

197
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:41,600
 notre générosité

198
00:05:41,600 --> 00:05:42,280
 comme communauté.

199
00:05:42,720 --> 00:05:43,780
 Ce qu'elle fait, Christine,

200
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:45,340
 avec ses 500 enfants,

201
00:05:45,740 --> 00:05:46,400
 c'est du miracle.

202
00:05:47,060 --> 00:05:47,980
 Alors, si on est tous là

203
00:05:47,980 --> 00:05:48,580
 en train de se dire

204
00:05:48,580 --> 00:05:49,300
 qu'on a beaucoup de problèmes

205
00:05:49,300 --> 00:05:49,720
 dans la vie,

206
00:05:50,160 --> 00:05:50,660
 allez lui parler

207
00:05:50,660 --> 00:05:51,500
 à Christine Richardson

208
00:05:51,500 --> 00:05:52,500
 et regardez comment

209
00:05:52,500 --> 00:05:53,200
 vous pouvez l'aider,

210
00:05:53,460 --> 00:05:54,620
 elle, à aider nos enfants

211
00:05:54,620 --> 00:05:55,480
 de nos communautés.

212
00:05:55,760 --> 00:05:56,240
 Je vous remercie.

213
00:05:57,960 --> 00:05:58,620
 Merci beaucoup,

214
00:05:58,720 --> 00:05:59,620
 M. Théodoresco.

215
00:06:00,200 --> 00:06:01,320
 Donc, tel qu'a mandé

216
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:02,040
 dans l'ordre du jour,

217
00:06:02,140 --> 00:06:03,000
 nous allons directement

